<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>Set &quot;_BESClient_Download_RetryMinutes&quot; to 1 min</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<P>This task sets the "_BESClient_Download_RetryMinutes" to 1 min on the client. This will cause the client to wait 1 min after a failed attempt at asking a relay for a download. If it fails again, the client will wait 2 min before trying again, then 4, then 8, then 16, etc... This does not relate to how long a download may actually take to complete, only what happens when a relay responds to a client that a download is not available. </P>
<P><A href="https://www.ibm.com/developerworks/community/wikis/home?lang=en#!/wiki/Tivoli%20Endpoint%20Manager/page/Configuration%20Settings"><FONT color=#000080>https://www.ibm.com/developerworks/community/wikis/home?lang=en#!/wiki/Tivoli%20Endpoint%20Manager/page/Configuration%20Settings</FONT></A></P>
<P>When the TEM Client fails to download a file from the TEM Server or a TEM Relay during an action, it will wait for the amount of time specified in the "_BESClient_Download_RetryMinutes"&nbsp;setting, then try again. After each failed attempt, it will double the retry time.</P>
<P>This setting used to have a default value of 1, but appears to now have a default value of 10, which means the client will by default wait a full 10 minutes before checking with the relay again if a download is available. This can significantly slow down the processing of baselines and other actions.</P>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>(if exists property &quot;in proxy agent context&quot; then ( not in proxy agent context ) else true )</Relevance>
    <Relevance>(not exists setting &quot;_BESClient_Download_RetryMinutes&quot; whose(&quot;1&quot; = value of it) of client)</Relevance>
    <Source>jgs194</Source>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2013-06-26</SourceReleaseDate>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Wed, 26 Jun 2013 15:17:15 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to deploy this action.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">setting &quot;_BESClient_Download_RetryMinutes&quot;=&quot;1&quot; on &quot;{parameter &quot;action issue date&quot; of action}&quot; for client
</ActionScript>
      <SuccessCriteria Option="OriginalRelevance"></SuccessCriteria>
    </DefaultAction>
  </Task>
</BES>
